   "evidence": "Upstream names the identical fact with the suffix: `Mathlib/Geometry/Euclidean/Angle/Unoriented/Basic.lean:134` `theorem angle_smul_right_of_pos (x y : V) {r : \u211d} (hr : 0 < r) : angle x (r \u2022 y) = angle x y` and :141 `angle_smul_left_of_pos`, with the distinct `angle_smul_left_of_neg` at :153 showing why the restriction belongs in the name.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Jets/Frame/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to `cosAngle_smul_left_of_pos` / `cosAngle_smul_right_of_pos`.",
   "issue": "`cosAngle_smul_left` and `cosAngle_smul_right` (lines 235, 241) hold only for `0 < c` but carry no `_of_pos`; the bare `_smul_left` name advertises an unconditional rewrite, and the statement is false for `c < 0` (the cosine flips sign).",
   "line": 235
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib's analogous names always carry the second operand: `Mathlib/Analysis/Complex/Trigonometric.lean:822` `cosh_sq_sub_sinh_sq`, `Mathlib/Geometry/Euclidean/Circumcenter.lean:369` `dist_circumcenter_sq_eq_sq_sub_circumradius`; naming doc: \"the name of theorem simply describes the conclusion\".",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Jets/Frame/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Name the operand, e.g. `spatialNorm_eq_sqrt_energy_sq_sub_bilin_self` (matching this file's own `bilin_spatial_spatial` prefix for a `g`-application), and likewise name the divisor in the decomposition lemma.",
   "issue": "`spatialNorm_eq_sqrt_energy_sq_sub` ends in a dangling `sub`: the subtrahend `g p p` is unnamed, so the name does not determine the conclusion. Same truncation in `energy_div_smul_add_spatial` (line 123), where the divisor `\u221a(g n n)` is unnamed.",
   "line": 205
  }
